## Checks

1. ci.yml select job — verified. Push uses `github.event.before`; PR uses `github.event.pull_request.base.sha`; a first push gives 40 zeros, which the script resolves to the merge base with `origin/master` (reachable because of `fetch-depth: 0`); a force push keeps the right range but can fail closed when the old head is unreachable. Script failure exits 2 and fails the select job, so the affected job never starts: fails closed. Matrix is an array of `{id}`; `if: needs.select.outputs.matrix != '[]'` skips an empty plan; the helpers run the real select run block on scratch repos and compare its ids to the script output as sets.
2. Coverage — F1 (blocker). Old step ran `pnpm test` = `turbo run test` over the whole workspace. The new union (packages Test filters + affected matrix) covers all 13 apps but misses 4 standalone packages with test scripts: packages/architecture-enforcement (about 30 test files), packages/knowledge-space-practice, packages/mastery-runtime-compat, packages/reading-advantage-scripts. No workspace package depends on them, so no job ever runs their tests. The plan records only `untested_apps=3` (apps). `reading-advantage` (mode excluded) is still planned for CI (CI-01d), so no app loses coverage.
3. Science CI gates — F3 (Nit). Three heavy-run invocations: monorepo root, root runner: 32 failed, 8 passed (cwd-based paths read `/home/daniebo/...`); package root with `vitest.unit.config.ts`: no test files found (config excludes `lib/ci-gates/**`); package root with `vitest.verification.config.ts`: 4 files, 40 passed, 0 failed, exit 0. The strategy records no invocation, and its guard-table shape fails. Step name `Test` and the regex `run:[^\n]*pnpm test` match the new ci.yml, and the passing phase-13 file asserts the real ci.yml content directly.
4. Services and env — verified. The affected job copies the packages job exactly: both DATABASE_URL values, both service containers with the same env and health checks, and `COMPANY_IDENTITY_TEST_POSTGRES_CONTAINER` on the run step.
5. Sales build identity — verified. `capture-company-candidate` sits after `verify-repair-verify-legacy-rollback` and before `update-traffic`; the script writes `<prefix>.revision` and fails closed on a wrong digest, a non-latest revision, or an unpublished URL; the move is a bash step with correct `$$` escapes, reads the candidate record with `--to-revisions=`, no tag, no legacy record. The push file holds `--tag=candidate`, so a later push makes the capture fail closed. The runbook matches.
6. Test meaning — verified. The Red cases build real scratch repos, run the real script and the real select block, compare sets, assert `changed_files>=1` before an empty plan (A4), use labeled counts (A3), and F-19 pins 10 labeled checks with a negative mutant. The Red logs record good-copy-passes and bad-copy-fails proofs.
7. Scope and truthfulness — verified with one Nit (F4). `p3_out_of_scope_paths=0` holds as a fact over the 7 P3 commits; the labeled line is absent from plan 3.4 evidence. Task 3.3 records master CI as failed (`Architecture boundary check`, run 41796713259) and never claims CI is green (A5 holds). The gate reproduces: exit 0, 130 of 130.

